(3860481, 546895, 63267, '<td valign="top">Shoehorn!  How does this relate to what you did this weekend?  You quote a song as your title and think it fits the challenge?  I don''t.  DNMC=1<br/> <br/>Edit;<br/>Although I don''t feel you met the spitir of the challenge, I do like how you have done the photo.  The red shows up very well and the lighting is creative.  If I felt this picture fit the challenge I would surely vote it at least a 7.  However since I don''t feel it fits the challenge, other then the word Weekend in the title, which I am giving credit for I am raising my initial vote from the DNMC=1 to a DNMC=5.</td>', 'Shoehorn!  How does this relate to what you did this weekend?  You quote a song as your title and think it fits the challenge?  I don''t.  DNMC=1 Edit;Although I don''t feel you met the spitir of the challenge, I do like how you have done the photo.  The red shows up very well and the lighting is creative.  If I felt this picture fit the challenge I would surely vote it at least a 7.  However since I don''t feel it fits the challenge, other then the word Weekend in the title, which I am giving credit for I am raising my initial vote from the DNMC=1 to a DNMC=5.', '2007-07-02 21:34:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(3860490, 545362, 63267, '<td valign="top">This relates to what you did this weekend how?  Sire it is a semi--humorous picture, but DNMC=1<br/> <br/>edit;<br/>After looking at the photo again, I can see how this could fit into your weeknd.  If you went bowling in the middle of the street on a drunken Saturday I could see how something like this could happen.  I do however still feel that you tried to shoehorn and interesting photo into the challenge.  Taking all of this into consideration I am raising my orginal DNMC=1 to a 5.</td>', 'This relates to what you did this weekend how?  Sire it is a semi--humorous picture, but DNMC=1 edit;After looking at the photo again, I can see how this could fit into your weeknd.  If you went bowling in the middle of the street on a drunken Saturday I could see how something like this could happen.  I do however still feel that you tried to shoehorn and interesting photo into the challenge.  Taking all of this into consideration I am raising my orginal DNMC=1 to a 5.', '2007-07-02 21:37:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(3860498, 546747, 63267, '<td valign="top">This relates to your weekend how?  Did you give birth to a colt?  What?  DNMC=1<br/> <br/>edit;<br/>I can understand how you travelling to take a picture of the colt would constitute something you did this weekend.  But I still think your title could have tied the colt into the challenge a little better.<br/> <br/>The photo itself is nice, though I find the rose bush a bit of a distraction from the colt.  The front hoof being clipped by the crop is also a hinderance.  The color and exposure is nice.  <br/> <br/>Since I still feel there is some DNMC in this photo, I am raising it from my DNMC=1 to a 5.  With the hoof and the rose shrub I would have voted it a 6, but am deducting slightly for the DNMC because I can see that some intent was there.</td>', 'This relates to your weekend how?  Did you give birth to a colt?  What?  DNMC=1 edit;I can understand how you travelling to take a picture of the colt would constitute something you did this weekend.  But I still think your title could have tied the colt into the challenge a little better. The photo itself is nice, though I find the rose bush a bit of a distraction from the colt.  The front hoof being clipped by the crop is also a hinderance.  The color and exposure is nice.   Since I still feel there is some DNMC in this photo, I am raising it from my DNMC=1 to a 5.  With the hoof and the rose shrub I would have voted it a 6, but am deducting slightly for the DNMC because I can see that some intent was there.', '2007-07-02 21:40:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(3860513, 546649, 63267, '<td valign="top">How does this relate to your weekend?  Is this you?  The blown out portions kill a photograph that was already shoehorned into this challenge.  DNMC=1<br/> <br/>edit;<br/>I am sensing that you went to a fair or a festival to take this photo.  In that sense I can see how this photo relates to your weekend.  I do wish that you had tied this into your title somehow.  the blown out highlights still detract from what is an interesting craftsman.<br/> <br/>Taking into consideration the phoito itself, I would have probably voted it a 6 with the highlights and lighting the way it is.  Because I feel you didn''t convey to me the challenge, I am upping my original DNMC=1 to a 5, but will not give you the 6 I would have otherwise voted.</td>', 'How does this relate to your weekend?  Is this you?  The blown out portions kill a photograph that was already shoehorned into this challenge.  DNMC=1 edit;I am sensing that you went to a fair or a festival to take this photo.  In that sense I can see how this photo relates to your weekend.  I do wish that you had tied this into your title somehow.  the blown out highlights still detract from what is an interesting craftsman. Taking into consideration the phoito itself, I would have probably voted it a 6 with the highlights and lighting the way it is.  Because I feel you didn''t convey to me the challenge, I am upping my original DNMC=1 to a 5, but will not give you the 6 I would have otherwise voted.', '2007-07-02 21:43:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(3860525, 546719, 63267, '<td valign="top">Shoehorn!  How does this fit into weekend?  I don''t know...DNMC=1<br/> <br/>edit;<br/>Looking at the photo and the title, I can loosely see how this fit your weekend.  I can read it as the deer are saying that you were sneaking up on them and in turn that would mean you snuck up on some deer tot photograph them this weekend.<br/> <br/>Overall the photo is delightful.  The lighting seems a bit off to me.  Almost as if it is missing some contrast.  The Sharpness seems more centered on the hind of the mother then on her face.<br/> <br/>Without taking DNMC into consideration I would have probably voted this a 6 because of the sharpness and lighting.  Adding the fact that the title didn''t convey the challenge theme to me very well, I will up my original DNMC=1 to a 5, but will not give the full 6 because I think your title could have done better.</td>', 'Shoehorn!  How does this fit into weekend?  I don''t know...DNMC=1 edit;Looking at the photo and the title, I can loosely see how this fit your weekend.  I can read it as the deer are saying that you were sneaking up on them and in turn that would mean you snuck up on some deer tot photograph them this weekend. Overall the photo is delightful.  The lighting seems a bit off to me.  Almost as if it is missing some contrast.  The Sharpness seems more centered on the hind of the mother then on her face. Without taking DNMC into consideration I would have probably voted this a 6 because of the sharpness and lighting.  Adding the fact that the title didn''t convey the challenge theme to me very well, I will up my original DNMC=1 to a 5, but will not give the full 6 because I think your title could have done better.', '2007-07-02 21:47:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(3860539, 545037, 63267, '<td valign="top">Shoehorn!  I don''t relate this image to the challenge.  Had you said you tested a new macro lens, or practiced macro photos, that would have helped, but simply submitting a macro photo and saying it was Macro weekend doesn''t work for me.  DNMC=1<br/> <br/>edit;<br/>I think I was a little harsh on my DNMC on this one.  Looking at it again I can see that you had a Macro Weekend.  That in itself should have sufficed.  I apologize for originally not giving this picture or title the credit it deserved.<br/> <br/>This is a great macro shot.  The pollen really makes it special.  I am upping my original DNMC=1 to an 8.  Best of luck to you on the challenge, and please accept my apologies.</td>', 'Shoehorn!  I don''t relate this image to the challenge.  Had you said you tested a new macro lens, or practiced macro photos, that would have helped, but simply submitting a macro photo and saying it was Macro weekend doesn''t work for me.  DNMC=1 edit;I think I was a little harsh on my DNMC on this one.  Looking at it again I can see that you had a Macro Weekend.  That in itself should have sufficed.  I apologize for originally not giving this picture or title the credit it deserved. This is a great macro shot.  The pollen really makes it special.  I am upping my original DNMC=1 to an 8.  Best of luck to you on the challenge, and please accept my apologies.', '2007-07-02 21:49:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(3860546, 546722, 9906, '<td valign="top">A landscape (unless it is a really potent, excellently executed landscape) still needs a subject to be a good photograph.  This by itself, while a nice peaceful scene, needs that subject to make it pop...<br/>TC</td>', 'A landscape (unless it is a really potent, excellently executed landscape) still needs a subject to be a good photograph.  This by itself, while a nice peaceful scene, needs that subject to make it pop...TC', '2007-07-02 21:50:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(3860549, 545885, 63267, '<td valign="top">How does this fit into your weekend?  Did you go swimming?  Did you go the beach or do you just live there?  Is that you on top of the diving board?  I see a picture that is SHOEHORNED!  DNMC=1<br/> <br/>edit;<br/>This is one of those tough ones that I looked at when I voted DNMC.  I can''t tell from the photo or title if this is something you did over the weekend.  I don''t know if you had to travel here, or if you live here.  I don''t know if you were on top of the tower, or if you just caught a picture of someone there.  What I do know is that I see a tower with someone up there and the words look before you leap which you have copied to make your title.<br/> <br/>I could have seen the theme if the title had said, looked before I lept or something like that, but I still just can''t fit it into the challenge.  <br/> <br/>Other then that I like the photo as far as the subject and the BW but I don''t like the woman being in color.  I think a bit more contrast could help this as well.</td>', 'How does this fit into your weekend?  Did you go swimming?  Did you go the beach or do you just live there?  Is that you on top of the diving board?  I see a picture that is SHOEHORNED!  DNMC=1 edit;This is one of those tough ones that I looked at when I voted DNMC.  I can''t tell from the photo or title if this is something you did over the weekend.  I don''t know if you had to travel here, or if you live here.  I don''t know if you were on top of the tower, or if you just caught a picture of someone there.  What I do know is that I see a tower with someone up there and the words look before you leap which you have copied to make your title. I could have seen the theme if the title had said, looked before I lept or something like that, but I still just can''t fit it into the challenge.   Other then that I like the photo as far as the subject and the BW but I don''t like the woman being in color.  I think a bit more contrast could help this as well.', '2007-07-02 21:52:51.000000', NULL, 1),
