(3884361, 546824, 21304, '<td valign="top">Awesome photo!! I had this one marked down in my thoughts as number 1 and I was close. Looks like we both had some pretty cool weekends you and I!</td>', 'Awesome photo!! I had this one marked down in my thoughts as number 1 and I was close. Looks like we both had some pretty cool weekends you and I!', '2007-07-09 02:40:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(3884382, 546588, 62187, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by BHuseman:</b></div><hr/><i> How does this relate to your weekend?  I see shoehorn, and DNMC=1<br/> <br/>edit,<br/>This is one where I still struggle with raising my vote.  Did you go snorkeling?  Maybe.  How can I tell though?  What this looks like to me is a man snorkeling in his studio.  the white background makes this shot look staged and therefore I can''t say you went snorkeling.  It looks like you pur your gear on, and took a studio photo.<br/> <br/>Overall this is very creative.  I am curious about the fish in the mask and how it was done.  the highkey works with the image, it just doesn''t convey your weekend to me.  If I didn''t feel this was a DNMC I would hve voted it an 8 easily.  I like it.<br/> <br/>However, I am still having a problem coming to grips with how it meets the challenge.  If I loosely say well the title doesn''t matter he went snorkeling, then it fits.  But I think in this challenge and for this image the title matters.  I am raising my original DNMC=1 to 5.  I would have gone higher if I didn''t think the title lets this image down, if only in the context of this challenge.  Had this been a free study the title would have fit perfectly.  But not in this challenge, in my opinion.  And I have to vote based on my opinion. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Well put and probably a feeling that most of us have. It just goes to prove that a great photo, no matter what the challenge, will almost certainly beat out a creative, but of lesser quality photo that totally meets the challenge and/or description of the challenge. It''s a puzzling fact to me and I''m glad you said it.</td>', 'Originally posted by BHuseman: How does this relate to your weekend?  I see shoehorn, and DNMC=1 edit,This is one where I still struggle with raising my vote.  Did you go snorkeling?  Maybe.  How can I tell though?  What this looks like to me is a man snorkeling in his studio.  the white background makes this shot look staged and therefore I can''t say you went snorkeling.  It looks like you pur your gear on, and took a studio photo. Overall this is very creative.  I am curious about the fish in the mask and how it was done.  the highkey works with the image, it just doesn''t convey your weekend to me.  If I didn''t feel this was a DNMC I would hve voted it an 8 easily.  I like it. However, I am still having a problem coming to grips with how it meets the challenge.  If I loosely say well the title doesn''t matter he went snorkeling, then it fits.  But I think in this challenge and for this image the title matters.  I am raising my original DNMC=1 to 5.  I would have gone higher if I didn''t think the title lets this image down, if only in the context of this challenge.  Had this been a free study the title would have fit perfectly.  But not in this challenge, in my opinion.  And I have to vote based on my opinion.   Well put and probably a feeling that most of us have. It just goes to prove that a great photo, no matter what the challenge, will almost certainly beat out a creative, but of lesser quality photo that totally meets the challenge and/or description of the challenge. It''s a puzzling fact to me and I''m glad you said it.', '2007-07-09 02:48:51.000000', NULL, 0),
